%N A122717 Least prime P such that P is the least of bemirps of n digits and the bemirps are first of twin primes or 0 if no such primes exist.
%C A122717 Bemirps: primes that yield a different prime when turned upside down with reversals of both being two more different primes (see A048895).
%C A122717 Every member of a twin bemirp group must end in 1 (bemirps begin and end with 1, see A048895), so a(n) has digits in {0,1,6,8,9} with first and last digit 1. The digit sum is unchanged by reversal and by swapping 6 and 9, so all four members are congruent mod 3; for each member and its +2 partner to be prime, the digit sum of a(n) must be 2 (mod 3). - _Jeff Sponaugle_, Nov 05 2026
%H A122717 Jeff Sponaugle, <a href="/A122717/b122717.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..30</a>
%H A122717 Chris Caldwell, <a href="https://t5k.org/glossary/page.php?sort=Bemirp">Bemirp</a>.
%e A122717 111696081881 and 111696081883 twin primes,
%e A122717 111969081881 and 111969081883 twin primes,
%e A122717 188180696111 and 188180696113 twin primes,
%e A122717 188180969111 and 188180969113 twin primes,
%e A122717 so the least bemirp 111696081881 = a(12).
%e A122717 a(15) = 106999008890801: 106999008890801, 108068800666901, 108098800999601 and 109666008860801 are bemirps and each plus 2 is prime.
%e A122717 a(16) = 1006089809099981: 1006089809099981, 1009086806066681, 1866606086809001 and 1899909089806001 are bemirps and each plus 2 is prime.
%e A122717 a(17) = 10008018816981191: 10008018816981191, 10008018819681161, 16118691881080001 and 19118961881080001 are bemirps and each plus 2 is prime.
%e A122717 a(18) = 100161686888168861: 100161686888168861, 100191989888198891, 168861888686161001 and 198891888989191001 are bemirps and each plus 2 is prime.
%o A122717 (PARI) \\ checks whether P is a term (P must also be the least such n-digit number)
%o A122717 isok(P) = my(v=digits(P), sw(w)=apply(d->if(d==6, 9, if(d==9, 6, d)), w), g=[P, fromdigits(sw(v)), fromdigits(Vecrev(v)), fromdigits(Vecrev(sw(v)))]); #Set(g)==4 && #setminus(Set(v), [0, 1, 6, 8, 9])==0 && vecmin(apply(x->isprime(x) && isprime(x+2), g)); \\ _Jeff Sponaugle_, Nov 05 2026
